The six-day protest by the Students’ Federation of India (SFI) and Democratic Youth Federation of India (DYFI) at Rajarathinam Stadium ended on Saturday with a victory march. While the parallel stir at the CPI state headquarters, Balan Illam, initially showed signs of continuation, with some of the agitators saying that they would carry on with their protest till NEET is completely banned, it was eventually called off around 11 pm.  The Rajarathinam Stadium protest, held in solidarity with the Cockroach Janata Party (CJP)-led nationwide agitation over the alleged NEET question paper leak, was called off on instructions from the organisations’ national committees following the withdrawal of protests in New Delhi, @SubashiniViji writes. 

